[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186100946 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9683153e-7324-5fb1-80ce-172326e0407d" "question-311d3c6d-fd7c-5156-9816-24d4c0a4cb73"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9683153e-7324-5fb1-80ce-172326e0407d" :question/id #uuid "9683153e-7324-5fb1-80ce-172326e0407d" :question/math-academy-id "q-87243" :question/problem "![](images/fa/fa8eef8fc185109d90dcc6c17f9684db06050d9b2cf63560186c45e8ce0ac204.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the function $y=f(x).$ Which of the following gives the graph of $y=f(3(x+2))?$" :question/worked-solution "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out horizontal stretches, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo plot $y=f(3(x+2)),$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Stretch it by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{(3)}=\\frac{1}{3}$ parallel to the $x$-axis to get the graph of $y=f(3x).$\n\n![](images/30/3027f0943e238d63996c8d1ff36d36b14bb60c18957168f7e54bb0a7ddcd9d33.png)\n\n  \n\n- Then, translate it left by $2$ units to get the graph of $y=f(3(x+2)).$\n\n![](images/e3/e3e552a5bacd539ee409a69be7e69cddc4e4e2404bcc4adc5173e980e8c8ca93.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b75424f3-f13f-5b3f-a284-ab8eea9d099c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b75424f3-f13f-5b3f-a284-ab8eea9d099c" :answer-field/id #uuid "b75424f3-f13f-5b3f-a284-ab8eea9d099c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f5e48cb0-af41-59b9-8d6c-47bcc06eafa9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-40e5f0af-4b75-5a30-a17d-4417edb56708" "answer-d376679e-80e4-5df5-aa72-5c8effe9d4b7" "answer-bcef57bc-48c4-5725-b238-e1b4e144afb3" "answer-f5e48cb0-af41-59b9-8d6c-47bcc06eafa9" "answer-b7b9f146-90ab-5464-a6ea-34df9c5dba5b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-40e5f0af-4b75-5a30-a17d-4417edb56708" :answer/id #uuid "40e5f0af-4b75-5a30-a17d-4417edb56708" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/34/343546800fc6ecd2945048933101bbbc19a73d4ac7e6a676a2cf46f9be70adf8.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d376679e-80e4-5df5-aa72-5c8effe9d4b7" :answer/id #uuid "d376679e-80e4-5df5-aa72-5c8effe9d4b7" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/62/624f7a53993bd26396aaa597669f2c3f44a03baf92e5c5da87a7f17ea5a83d4a.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bcef57bc-48c4-5725-b238-e1b4e144afb3" :answer/id #uuid "bcef57bc-48c4-5725-b238-e1b4e144afb3" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/6c/6cf121bb9b724d0367eab935b03dd51f46fa0c279906c06a9bdfc96e6c79f369.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5e48cb0-af41-59b9-8d6c-47bcc06eafa9" :answer/id #uuid "f5e48cb0-af41-59b9-8d6c-47bcc06eafa9" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/77/77c4c913c552c4560b4f22a6ac07726adb6a4d99450db3862412ea96a11f1d2a.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b7b9f146-90ab-5464-a6ea-34df9c5dba5b" :answer/id #uuid "b7b9f146-90ab-5464-a6ea-34df9c5dba5b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/fa/fa8eef8fc185109d90dcc6c17f9684db06050d9b2cf63560186c45e8ce0ac204.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186101561 :question/problem "![](images/64/642590d3e04de8365075f79f7954c5123019326b1f4addc618a9a2f54a09e881.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the function $y=f(x).$ Which of the following gives the graph of $y=f(x-1)+3?$" :question/worked-solution "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out horizontal stretches, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo plot $y=f(x-1)+3,$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Translate it right by $1$ unit to get the graph of $y=f(x-1).$\n\n![](images/da/da5e6848776232c4f4429c8b3c5e3fdaaae2e9a99a180dfe409893e97d407036.png)\n\n- Then, translate it up by $3$ units to get the graph of $y=f(x-1)+3.$\n\n![](images/81/8188a686d0f9c579f44601645667c0209a39b6500864eb9479147940ef1ebb26.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186100527 :answer-field/correct 17592186100531 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-311d3c6d-fd7c-5156-9816-24d4c0a4cb73" :question/id #uuid "311d3c6d-fd7c-5156-9816-24d4c0a4cb73" :question/math-academy-id "q-112634" :question/problem "![](images/ec/ec193bb78fbfb43cec5266622ef0bef14e6aad5798687ae9c7cc7233e69078cb.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the function $y=f(x).$ Which of the following gives the graph of $y=f(3(x-5))?$" :question/worked-solution "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out horizontal stretches, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo plot $y=f(3(x-5)),$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Stretch it by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{(3)}=\\frac{1}{3}$ parallel to the $x$-axis to get the graph of $y=f(3x).$\n\n![](images/c4/c41d06f741882e3993ebe8eb7eab5c42c362d3c11b9b8ad1e4fed983498c95d0.png)\n\n- Then, translate it right by $5$ units to get the graph of $y=f(3(x-5)).$\n\n![](images/47/47bf38d228b4337b870baf777c53fbab43743f155f4a23aa6d0e2bd1f5bc45ad.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fa09890c-3a44-50c2-b038-e436dbd0b29c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fa09890c-3a44-50c2-b038-e436dbd0b29c" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa09890c-3a44-50c2-b038-e436dbd0b29c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2063484c-96a8-5c06-bd28-f076ec33f08c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2063484c-96a8-5c06-bd28-f076ec33f08c" "answer-d7d03033-d79c-5acc-9d9a-2046cbf19feb" "answer-fd9599ea-f6e5-5373-b3ba-146eb8b30782" "answer-8cbcc19b-28b6-5bd8-8f5c-4c8722e65c0d" "answer-03bfc5d5-8208-5f39-8039-f35d61e04db4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2063484c-96a8-5c06-bd28-f076ec33f08c" :answer/id #uuid "2063484c-96a8-5c06-bd28-f076ec33f08c" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/1a/1a832c774aeb07399060817149462c2e11c3313d5ad14816a8b6092abfef702b.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d7d03033-d79c-5acc-9d9a-2046cbf19feb" :answer/id #uuid "d7d03033-d79c-5acc-9d9a-2046cbf19feb" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/1e/1ee5948af075803bbab3e22ce9d22532cd8aa4e73679c01a93205e45311aa25c.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd9599ea-f6e5-5373-b3ba-146eb8b30782" :answer/id #uuid "fd9599ea-f6e5-5373-b3ba-146eb8b30782" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/a4/a4dd99ebd96ecf960998264b8defb7b9f27bd1c411aa2cea6d257c5182ac7fc1.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8cbcc19b-28b6-5bd8-8f5c-4c8722e65c0d" :answer/id #uuid "8cbcc19b-28b6-5bd8-8f5c-4c8722e65c0d" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/a9/a917739154143a16c1c5d76948d0392ce7376be034a9ca6e162cfd829594c2a7.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03bfc5d5-8208-5f39-8039-f35d61e04db4" :answer/id #uuid "03bfc5d5-8208-5f39-8039-f35d61e04db4" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/df/dfe8088aa2f2b09841223574c813c9197c29134eb9503e1697e852cd7184514f.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-d24b7158-f960-57fe-bd31-a6935529e708" :activity/id #uuid "d24b7158-f960-57fe-bd31-a6935529e708" :activity/title "Combining Graph Transformations: Two Operations" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050085 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-0b8293c3-52d1-5621-abf8-52fde1e15572" "step-7d9227a6-c2b7-5b74-9e9f-8551f850121c" "step-f7d4e6ad-eb99-5709-b8bf-9064ece78df6"] :activity/first-step "step-0b8293c3-52d1-5621-abf8-52fde1e15572" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-0b8293c3-52d1-5621-abf8-52fde1e15572" :step/id #uuid "0b8293c3-52d1-5621-abf8-52fde1e15572" :step/content "question-9683153e-7324-5fb1-80ce-172326e0407d" :step/next "step-7d9227a6-c2b7-5b74-9e9f-8551f850121c" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-7d9227a6-c2b7-5b74-9e9f-8551f850121c" :step/id #uuid "7d9227a6-c2b7-5b74-9e9f-8551f850121c" :step/content 17592186101561 :step/next "step-f7d4e6ad-eb99-5709-b8bf-9064ece78df6" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-f7d4e6ad-eb99-5709-b8bf-9064ece78df6" :step/id #uuid "f7d4e6ad-eb99-5709-b8bf-9064ece78df6" :step/content "question-311d3c6d-fd7c-5156-9816-24d4c0a4cb73" :db/ensure [:step/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-9683153e-7324-5fb1-80ce-172326e0407d" :question/id #uuid "9683153e-7324-5fb1-80ce-172326e0407d"] ["question-9683153e-7324-5fb1-80ce-172326e0407d" :question/math-academy-id "q-87243"] ["question-9683153e-7324-5fb1-80ce-172326e0407d" :question/problem "![](images/fa/fa8eef8fc185109d90dcc6c17f9684db06050d9b2cf63560186c45e8ce0ac204.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the function $y=f(x).$ Which of the following gives the graph of $y=f(3(x+2))?$"] ["question-9683153e-7324-5fb1-80ce-172326e0407d" :question/worked-solution "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out horizontal stretches, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo plot $y=f(3(x+2)),$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Stretch it by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{(3)}=\\frac{1}{3}$ parallel to the $x$-axis to get the graph of $y=f(3x).$\n\n![](images/30/3027f0943e238d63996c8d1ff36d36b14bb60c18957168f7e54bb0a7ddcd9d33.png)\n\n  \n\n- Then, translate it left by $2$ units to get the graph of $y=f(3(x+2)).$\n\n![](images/e3/e3e552a5bacd539ee409a69be7e69cddc4e4e2404bcc4adc5173e980e8c8ca93.png)"] ["question-9683153e-7324-5fb1-80ce-172326e0407d" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-b75424f3-f13f-5b3f-a284-ab8eea9d099c" :answer-field/id #uuid "b75424f3-f13f-5b3f-a284-ab8eea9d099c"] ["answer-40e5f0af-4b75-5a30-a17d-4417edb56708" :answer/id #uuid "40e5f0af-4b75-5a30-a17d-4417edb56708"] ["answer-40e5f0af-4b75-5a30-a17d-4417edb56708" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-40e5f0af-4b75-5a30-a17d-4417edb56708" :answer/value "images/34/343546800fc6ecd2945048933101bbbc19a73d4ac7e6a676a2cf46f9be70adf8.png"] ["answer-d376679e-80e4-5df5-aa72-5c8effe9d4b7" :answer/id #uuid "d376679e-80e4-5df5-aa72-5c8effe9d4b7"] ["answer-d376679e-80e4-5df5-aa72-5c8effe9d4b7" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-d376679e-80e4-5df5-aa72-5c8effe9d4b7" :answer/value "images/62/624f7a53993bd26396aaa597669f2c3f44a03baf92e5c5da87a7f17ea5a83d4a.png"] ["answer-bcef57bc-48c4-5725-b238-e1b4e144afb3" :answer/id #uuid "bcef57bc-48c4-5725-b238-e1b4e144afb3"] ["answer-bcef57bc-48c4-5725-b238-e1b4e144afb3" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-bcef57bc-48c4-5725-b238-e1b4e144afb3" :answer/value "images/6c/6cf121bb9b724d0367eab935b03dd51f46fa0c279906c06a9bdfc96e6c79f369.png"] ["answer-f5e48cb0-af41-59b9-8d6c-47bcc06eafa9" :answer/id #uuid "f5e48cb0-af41-59b9-8d6c-