ctions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out horizontal stretches, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo plot $y=f(x-1)+3,$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Translate it right by $1$ unit to get the graph of $y=f(x-1).$\n\n![](images/da/da5e6848776232c4f4429c8b3c5e3fdaaae2e9a99a180dfe409893e97d407036.png)\n\n- Then, translate it up by $3$ units to get the graph of $y=f(x-1)+3.$\n\n![](images/81/8188a686d0f9c579f44601645667c0209a39b6500864eb9479147940ef1ebb26.png)"] [17592186101561 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [17592186100527 :answer-field/correct 17592186100531] ["question-311d3c6d-fd7c-5156-9816-24d4c0a4cb73" :question/id #uuid "311d3c6d-fd7c-5156-9816-24d4c0a4cb73"] ["question-311d3c6d-fd7c-5156-9816-24d4c0a4cb73" :question/math-academy-id "q-112634"] ["question-311d3c6d-fd7c-5156-9816-24d4c0a4cb73" :question/problem "![](images/ec/ec193bb78fbfb43cec5266622ef0bef14e6aad5798687ae9c7cc7233e69078cb.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the function $y=f(x).$ Which of the following gives the graph of $y=f(3(x-5))?$"] ["question-311d3c6d-fd7c-5156-9816-24d4c0a4cb73" :question/worked-solution "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out horizontal stretches, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo plot $y=f(3(x-5)),$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Stretch it by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{(3)}=\\frac{1}{3}$ parallel to the $x$-axis to get the graph of $y=f(3x).$\n\n![](images/c4/c41d06f741882e3993ebe8eb7eab5c42c362d3c11b9b8ad1e4fed983498c95d0.png)\n\n- Then, translate it right by $5$ units to get the graph of $y=f(3(x-5)).$\n\n![](images/47/47bf38d228b4337b870baf777c53fbab43743f155f4a23aa6d0e2bd1f5bc45ad.png)"] ["question-311d3c6d-fd7c-5156-9816-24d4c0a4cb73" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-fa09890c-3a44-50c2-b038-e436dbd0b29c" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa09890c-3a44-50c2-b038-e436dbd0b29c"] ["answer-2063484c-96a8-5c06-bd28-f076ec33f08c" :answer/id #uuid "2063484c-96a8-5c06-bd28-f076ec33f08c"] ["answer-2063484c-96a8-5c06-bd28-f076ec33f08c" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-2063484c-96a8-5c06-bd28-f076ec33f08c" :answer/value "images/1a/1a832c774aeb07399060817149462c2e11c3313d5ad14816a8b6092abfef702b.png"] ["answer-d7d03033-d79c-5acc-9d9a-2046cbf19feb" :answer/id #uuid "d7d03033-d79c-5acc-9d9a-2046cbf19feb"] ["answer-d7d03033-d79c-5acc-9d9a-2046cbf19feb" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-d7d03033-d79c-5acc-9d9a-2046cbf19feb" :answer/value "images/1e/1ee5948af075803bbab3e22ce9d22532cd8aa4e73679c01a93205e45311aa25c.png"] ["answer-fd9599ea-f6e5-5373-b3ba-146eb8b30782" :answer/id #uuid "fd9599ea-f6e5-5373-b3ba-146eb8b30782"] ["answer-fd9599ea-f6e5-5373-b3ba-146eb8b30782" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-fd9599ea-f6e5-5373-b3ba-146eb8b30782" :answer/value "images/a4/a4dd99ebd96ecf960998264b8defb7b9f27bd1c411aa2cea6d257c5182ac7fc1.png"] ["answer-8cbcc19b-28b6-5bd8-8f5c-4c8722e65c0d" :answer/id #uuid "8cbcc19b-28b6-5bd8-8f5c-4c8722e65c0d"] ["answer-8cbcc19b-28b6-5bd8-8f5c-4c8722e65c0d" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-8cbcc19b-28b6-5bd8-8f5c-4c8722e65c0d" :answer/value "images/a9/a917739154143a16c1c5d76948d0392ce7376be034a9ca6e162cfd829594c2a7.png"] ["answer-03bfc5d5-8208-5f39-8039-f35d61e04db4" :answer/id #uuid "03bfc5d5-8208-5f39-8039-f35d61e04db4"] ["answer-03bfc5d5-8208-5f39-8039-f35d61e04db4" :answer/type :answer.type/image